      "Instructions": "# Unioil-SF Database Analysis \u0026 Usage Skill\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nThis skill provides insight into the \\unioil-sf\\ database, specifically identifying active vs. legacy objects and mapping the relationships between core business entities.\r\n\r\n## Active Business Objects\r\nThese objects are critical for tracking sales performance, lead conversion, and operational activity:\r\n- **Lead**: Actively used for pipeline management, particularly for the **Fleet Card** segment. Contains detailed prospect information, volume projections, and conversion status.\r\n- **Account**: The central hub for all customer records.\r\n- **Opportunity_Sales_Order__c**: The primary source for transaction data. Use this instead of the deprecated \\Opportunity\\ table.\r\n- **Opportunity_Sales_Order_Line_Item__c**: Provides detailed product/volume breakdowns per transaction.\r\n- **Material__c**: The product master table.\r\n- **Blanket_Purchase_Orders__c**: Tracks long-term customer commitments.\r\n- **ATL_ATW__c \u0026 ATL_ATW_Line_Items__c**: Used for operational Authority to Load/Withdraw processes.\r\n\r\n## Legacy \u0026 Unused Objects\r\nThese tables are either deprecated, system-specific, or do not contain actionable business data:\r\n- **Opportunity**: **Deprecated.** Contains legacy records with missing \\Amount\\ data and no linked line items. All current reporting should ignore this table.\r\n- **LEXMAGICMOVER__* (All tables)**: System tables related to legacy Salesforce Lightning migration tools.\r\n- **SFGA__* (All tables)**: System tables related to Google Ads integration. Likely not used for internal performance analytics.\r\n- **Campaign / CampaignMember**: Standard CRM objects that appear to have limited or no integration with the current sales-focused reporting pipeline.\r\n\r\n## Relationship Mapping\r\nTo analyze performance, use the following join paths:\r\n1. **Lead to Account**: \\Lead.ConvertedAccountId\\ -\u003E \\Account.SalesforceId\\\r\n2. **Account to Sales Order**: \\Account.SalesforceId\\ -\u003E \\Opportunity_Sales_Order__c.AccountId\\\r\n3. **Sales Order to Line Items**: \\Opportunity_Sales_Order__c.SalesforceId\\ -\u003E \\Opportunity_Sales_Order_Line_Item__c.Opportunity_Sales_Order__c\\\r\n4. **Line Item to Material**: \\Opportunity_Sales_Order_Line_Item__c.Material__c\\ -\u003E \\Material__c.SalesforceId\\\r\n\r\n## Analytical Best Practices\r\n- **Transaction Data**: Always pull volume and revenue from \\Opportunity_Sales_Order__c\\ using the \\Total_Amount_VAT_Inc__c\\ field. The \\Total_Amount__c\\ field is not populated.\r\n- **Performance Monitoring**: Focus on 8-week rolling averages for top 5 accounts: METRO OIL SUBIC INC., SEAOIL PHILIPPINES, INC., POWERZONE PETROLEUM PRODUCTS CORPORATION, ONE SOURCE FUEL MARKETING CORP., and UNO FUEL, INC.",
